{"changes":["eka-cli (stage a): `eka verify [--changed] [--base \u003cref\u003e] [--json] [--force]` with a built-in check registry (agents-md-drift, snapshot-integrity, conformance, and the later scope-declarations). Exit 0 pass / 1 blocking violation / 2 usage-IO. Warnings never block. A violation carries the constraint id, the file and line, what is required, and the `eka get \u003cconstraint\u003e` command. Deterministic JSON names each check, its verdict and the constraint id.","Standard 1.6 (new): the distributed `templates/hooks/pre-commit` and `templates/hooks/pre-push` now invoke `eka verify --changed` (pre-commit vs HEAD, pre-push vs upstream), non-blocking by default; blocking only when the operator sets EKA_VERIFY_STRICT=1, preserving the 1.2 universal-capture contract.","Cascade: eka-core v1.12.1 (SpecificationVersion 1.6, accepts 1.5 at import), eka-cli v1.25.0 (re-vendored EKA + hooks from standard v1.6, re-pinned vendored.yaml, core v1.12.1), eka-mcp v1.15.5 (core v1.12.1).","CI wiring: the repository-scope verify runs in the cli quality pipeline (.anvil/pipelines/ci.yaml, stage `verify`), so the gate is enforced in CI as well as at the hook."],"role":"implementation","summary":"M3a (sto:verify-changed-gate) is complete. `eka verify [--changed]` runs the repository-scope checks the standards declare, reports a violation like a failing test (constraint id, file, line, the requirement, and the exact `eka get` command), and is installed at the git boundary where every host passes through. Stage (a) — the executor and its CI wiring — shipped earlier; stage (b) closes the acceptance criterion that the pre-commit and pre-push hook templates call it, delivered as EKA Standard 1.6 (the hook templates are standard artifacts).","tests":["eka-cli: go test ./cmd/ (verify suite) and `anvil pipeline ci` (11m41s) PASS; `eka verify` prints Checks: agents-md-drift/snapshot-integrity/conformance/scope-declarations [PASS], Verdict PASS.","eka-core: exchange import-acceptance test widened to 1.5 (a 1.6 importer reads every accepted line); ci PASS; release v1.12.1.","eka-mcp: full `go test ./...` PASS after core v1.12.1; ci PASS; release v1.15.5.","Hooks: `sh -n` clean on both templates; the eka-cli repo's .git/hooks symlinks point at the re-vendored templates, so the repository dogfoods the new gate."]}